4. Trivy Filesystem Scan

The simplest scan is:

	trivy fs .

This scans the current project directory.

Example:

	cd app

	trivy fs .

-------------------------------------------------------------------

5. Scan Only HIGH and CRITICAL

	In a CI/CD pipeline, you may want to focus on serious vulnerabilities:

	trivy fs \
	  --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
  .

	This is useful for Jenkins security gates.

-------------------------------------------------------------

6. Fail the Build for CRITICAL Vulnerabilities

	This is one of the most important concepts.

Use:

	trivy fs \
	  --severity CRITICAL \
	  --exit-code 1 \
	  .

What does --exit-code 1 do?

If Trivy finds a matching vulnerability:

	CRITICAL vulnerability found
	        ↓
	exit code = 1
	        ↓
	Jenkins detects failure
	        ↓
	BUILD FAILED


If nothing is found:

	No CRITICAL vulnerabilities
	        ↓
	exit code = 0
	        ↓
	Jenkins continues

This turns security scanning into a quality/security gate.

---------------------------------------------------------------


7. Docker Image Scanning

	First build your image:

	docker build -t myapp:latest .

Check:

	docker images

Then scan:

	trivy image myapp:latest


For HIGH and CRITICAL:

	trivy image \
	  --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
	  myapp:latest

Fail the build for CRITICAL:

	trivy image \
	  --severity CRITICAL \
	  --exit-code 1 \
	  myapp:latest


